            - strong [ref=e26]: "About Sezzle:"
          - paragraph [ref=e27]: With a mission to financially empower the next generation, Sezzle is revolutionizing the shopping experience beyond payments, blending cutting-edge tech with seamless, interest-free installment plans that make shopping smarter and more accessible. We’re not just transforming payments; we’re redefining how people discover, interact with, and purchase the things they love while driving real impact on merchant sales through increased conversions and higher order values. As we continue to shape the future of fintech and retail, we’re building an innovative, dynamic team passionate about creating more than just a transaction but a truly unique shopping journey. If you’re excited about pushing boundaries in tech and delivering a game-changing experience for consumers and merchants alike, come join us at Sezzle and help create the future of shopping!
          - paragraph [ref=e28]:
            - strong [ref=e30]: "About the Role:"
          - paragraph [ref=e31]:
            - generic [ref=e32]:
              - text: We are seeking a talented and motivated
              - strong [ref=e33]: AI Engineer I
              - text: who is best in class, with a high IQ and a high EQ. This role presents an exciting opportunity to thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced environment within a rapidly growing team, with strong prospects for continued growth and increased ownership.
          - paragraph [ref=e34]: As an AI Engineer I on the Applied AI team, you will contribute to the development of platforms and systems that power Sezzle's AI-driven capabilities. Your work will span initiatives such as building AI-powered features, developing intelligent automation and agentic systems, and embedding AI solutions into customer-facing products, internal tools, and operational workflows.
          - paragraph [ref=e35]: You will work closely with senior engineers and cross-functional teams to identify opportunities where AI can drive meaningful impact—whether that's enhancing the customer experience, improving decision-making, or automating complex workflows. This role is ideal for engineers early in their AI careers who want hands-on exposure to production-grade AI systems, with opportunities to grow into greater ownership and technical leadership over time.
          - paragraph [ref=e36]:
            - strong [ref=e38]: "What You'll Do:"
          - list [ref=e39]:
            - listitem [ref=e40]: Contribute to the design and development of AI-powered platforms and systems, working alongside senior engineers on complex initiatives.
            - listitem [ref=e41]: Own end-to-end delivery of complex projects, from problem discovery and system design through production rollout and iteration.
            - listitem [ref=e42]: Build AI-driven features, intelligent automation, and agentic systems that enhance customer experiences and improve team productivity.
            - listitem [ref=e43]: Embed AI capabilities into existing team workflows, products, and processes, ensuring solutions integrate naturally
            - listitem [ref=e44]: Integrate AI capabilities into customer-facing products, internal tools, and operational workflows.
            - listitem [ref=e45]: Build full-stack components spanning backend services, APIs, data layers, and frontend interfaces.
            - listitem [ref=e46]: Translate business and operational problems into maintainable, AI-enabled technical solutions with guidance from senior team members.
            - listitem [ref=e47]: Apply systems thinking to ensure reliability, performance, and security across platforms.
            - listitem [ref=e48]: Collaborate with engineers, teams, and stakeholders across the company to understand requirements and deliver impactful solutions.
            - listitem [ref=e49]: Participate in production support and incident response for team-owned systems, learning operational best practices.
            - listitem [ref=e50]: Engage in code reviews and knowledge sharing to continuously improve skills and contribute to team growth.
          - heading "What We'll Look For:" [level=3] [ref=e51]:
