                - text: into production environments.
            - listitem [ref=e61]: Strong proficiency in Python, SQL, and frontend frameworks such as React.
            - listitem [ref=e62]: Proven experience designing and owning production-grade full-stack systems.
            - listitem [ref=e63]: Experience working with distributed systems, internal platforms, or complex data workflows.
            - listitem [ref=e64]: Demonstrated experience working with Claude or equivalent large language model tools is required; candidates must be comfortable leveraging AI to enhance productivity, research, and communication.
            - listitem [ref=e65]: Ability to operate effectively in ambiguous problem spaces and drive solutions with minimal direction.
          - heading "Preferred Qualifications:" [level=3] [ref=e66]:
            - strong [ref=e68]: "Preferred Qualifications:"
          - list [ref=e69]:
            - listitem [ref=e70]: Exposure to building AI-powered platforms or products, including contributing to architectural decisions.
            - listitem [ref=e71]: Foundational knowledge of core machine learning and data science principles, including supervised/unsupervised learning, feature engineering, and model evaluation.
            - listitem [ref=e72]: Familiarity with transformer architectures (BERT, GPT, etc.) and basic understanding of attention mechanisms, tokenization, and fine-tuning concepts.
            - listitem [ref=e73]: Exposure to embeddings and vector representations, including text embeddings and similarity search concepts; interest in vector databases (Pinecone, Weaviate, pgvector, or similar).
            - listitem [ref=e74]: Familiarity with NLP techniques such as text classification, named entity recognition, or semantic search.
            - listitem [ref=e75]: Familiarity with real-world agentic frameworks workflow engines (e.g., in-house automation platforms, langchain/graph, n8n, Make, or similar), with a solid understanding of how they work under the hood.
            - listitem [ref=e76]: Experience developing AI-assisted or agentic systems that interact with tools, data, or workflows.
            - listitem [ref=e77]: Familiarity with cloud-native development using AWS.
            - listitem [ref=e78]: Experience with containerized systems and orchestration tools such as Docker and Kubernetes.
            - listitem [ref=e79]: Exposure to CI/CD pipelines and modern development workflows (e.g., GitLab).
            - listitem [ref=e80]: Experience with Golang is a plus (or willingness to learn).
